set.body:
Migrate CPCA and supervised-plan consumers onto Op, OperatorProgram, FunctionalFrame, and the shared result contract.

Scope:
- CPCA planners and estimator adapters;
- CPCA constraint representation and local ROI executor resolution;
- planned versus fitted artifact boundaries;
- typed row relations and feature operators used by CPCA;
- removal of CPCA-specific dependencies on MvMetric, MvMap, DualityDiagram, and raw GenPca.

Preserve the current public scientific behavior while replacing the compute path. Compatibility adapters may exist only as thin delegates and must be named for deletion by the purge issue.

Acceptance:
- existing CPCA scenario and adapter suites pass on JVM and JS;
- independent dense/analytic fixtures verify operator construction and reported components;
- invalid constraint combinations remain unrepresentable or return a typed error;
- no densification or JVM-only dependency appears in shared code;
- the legacy-consumer inventory marks every CPCA entry migrated.
